course: dictionary
lesson: 7649
title: Learning the word projector
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A projector is a machine that makes a picture much bigger by shining light so the image lands on a screen or wall. You can find the meaning from the clues around the word. «Turn on the projector» tells you it is a machine you switch on, and «overhead projector» and «film projector» show it is a type of machine that shows pictures.
explain: The eclipse sentences show a safe use. «You must never look at a solar eclipse with your bare eyes or ordinary sunglasses» tells you looking straight at the Sun is dangerous. Then «use proper eclipse glasses or a pinhole projector» gives the safe choice. A pinhole projector lets you see the Sun's picture without looking at the Sun itself.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Use proper eclipse glasses or a machine that shows the picture» still makes sense, so projector fits. Word clues and a quick swap help you understand new words.
fact: A projector is a machine that shines light to show a large image on a screen or wall.
fact: In school, a projector is often fixed to the ceiling and connected to a computer or interactive whiteboard.
fact: Teachers use projectors to show slides and videos.
fact: «Overhead projector» and «film projector» are two kinds you may hear about.
fact: A pinhole projector shows the Sun's image safely, because you never look at a solar eclipse with your bare eyes.
exercise: «Teachers turn on the projector to show slides on the wall.» What is a projector? | *A machine that shows a large image on a screen or wall | A small pencil case | A kind of fish that lives in the sea | A type of sunglasses for bright days
exercise: «Use a pinhole projector instead of looking at the Sun.» Why is a pinhole projector used during an eclipse? | It is a loud musical instrument | *It is a safe way to see the Sun's image without looking straight at it | It keeps your hands warm | It makes the Sun go dark
exercise: «The film projector clicked in the dark room.» Find and copy the word that names a machine. | film | *projector | room | clicked
test: In a science lesson, a projector shows how a lens bends light to make an image bigger. What does the projector do in this lesson? | *It makes an image bigger on a screen | It cooks food for the class | It measures how heavy a lens is
test: Where would you most likely find a projector at school? | *Fixed to the ceiling of a classroom | Buried under the playground | Folded up small in the school kitchen | Inside a bag of school books
exam: Which is a safe way to watch a solar eclipse? | *Use a pinhole projector | Stare at it through a window | Look straight at it with your bare eyes | Wear ordinary sunglasses
